# Hello World

## Purpose

This is the smallest program in the collection. It writes the text `Hello
World!` to the terminal, demonstrating how to run a Python file and display
text with the built-in `print` function.

## Requirements

- Python 3
- No third-party packages

## Run

From this folder, run:

```text
python hello_world.py
```

Expected output:

```text
Hello World!
```

## How it works

`print` receives one string and writes it to standard output, followed by a
newline. Python executes this statement when the script is run.

## Flow diagram

```text
Start
  |
  v
Call print("Hello World!")
  |
  v
Write greeting to terminal
  |
  v
End
```
